# Copy to demo.env (not committed) and list the demo agents in call order.
# Each entry: namespace/serviceaccount[=Display Name]. Use quotes; separate entries with spaces;
# display names must not contain spaces (use Research-Agent, not "Research Agent").
DEMO_USER=alice
DEMO_AGENTS="agents/planner=Planner agents/researcher=Researcher tools/mcp-client=MCP-Client"
# Optional:
# IMAGE=registry.example.com/demo/otel-spiffe-python:1   # image with the Python libs preinstalled (disconnected)
# OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector.tracing.svc.cluster.local:4318
# Scales the staged timing of each agent's steps (1.0 = about 3-5 s per agent).
#DEMO_PACE=1.0
# Optional: the last agent makes one real MCP tool call through the MCP gateway, as its own
# service account. Unset = no MCP step. "$NS" in the arguments becomes the agent's namespace.
#DEMO_MCP_TOOL=openshift_pods_list_in_namespace
#DEMO_MCP_ARGS='{"namespace":"$NS"}'   # single quotes: this file is sourced by bash
# Defaults: the in-cluster gateway Service, and Host mcp.<apps domain>.
#DEMO_MCP_URL=http://mcp-gateway-openshift-default.openshift-ingress.svc.cluster.local:8080/mcp
#DEMO_MCP_HOST=mcp.apps.example.com
# Optional: one more hop after the last agent, run as THIS service account, making the same tool
# call again. The account must have no RBAC (oc create sa NAME -n NS, no RoleBindings), so the
# MCP server refuses it; the trace shows the refusal next to the allowed call. Needs DEMO_MCP_TOOL.
#DEMO_MCP_CONTRAST=agents/demo-no-rbac=No-RBAC
# Optional: after its steps, the last agent sends one real request to OGX (POST <url>/v1/responses),
# so the trace continues into OGX's spans. The URL is the OGX server (route or in-cluster Service).
# The token must be a Keycloak token with the ogx-api audience (10-ogx.yaml accepts no other
# issuer): get one with scripts/lib-oc-token.sh (rhoai-mass-aws) or your Keycloak token endpoint.
# It is passed to the probe pod and never printed. Unset DEMO_OGX_TOKEN and the request goes
# unauthenticated, which an OGX with auth on refuses with 401 — the span shows the refusal.
#DEMO_OGX_URL=http://ogx-server.agents.svc.cluster.local:8321
#DEMO_OGX_MODEL=publishers/llm/models/qwen3-8b
#DEMO_OGX_TOKEN=<keycloak-user-token>
# With DEMO_OGX_URL set, DEMO_OGX_MCP=1 also hands OGX the MCP gateway as a tool server, so OGX
# produces list_mcp_tools and invoke_mcp_tool spans. OGX's service account then needs the same
# gateway RBAC the agents have.
#DEMO_OGX_MCP=1
